course: dictionary
lesson: 6145
title: Big time words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words measure very long periods of time. A decade is 10 years, a century is 100 years, and a millennium is 1,000 years. «Big stretches of time have names: a decade is 10 years, a century 100 years and a millennium 1,000 years.» So a millennium is ten hundreds of years.
explain: The plural is millennia, or sometimes millenniums. You will often see millennia when someone talks about a very long time. «Valleys are carved slowly over millennia» means over many thousands of years.
explain: Context can help you here too. «No person lives a millennium, though some bristlecone pine trees in the USA are over 4,000 years old.» The oldest people live about 120 years, so a millennium is much longer than any human life. You can work out the meaning from the clues.
explain: Millennium can also mean the moment a new thousand years starts, as in «the turn of the millennium». Big parties and fireworks often mark it.
fact: A millennium is a period of a thousand years.
fact: A decade is 10 years, a century is 100 years, and a millennium is 1,000 years.
fact: The plural of millennium is millennia (or millenniums).
fact: «The millennium» often means the moment a new thousand years starts in the calendar.
fact: People can disagree about exactly when a new millennium begins: «the new millennium really began in 2001, not at the huge parties of 2000», says one picky grandad.
exercise: «No person lives a millennium.» How many years is a millennium? | *1,000 years | 120 years | 10 years | 100 years
exercise: «Big stretches of time have names: a decade is 10 years, a century 100 years.» How many years is a century? | 1,000 | 10 | 4,000 | *100
exercise: «Valleys are carved slowly over millennia.» What does millennia mean here? | A small party | A type of fireworks | A single year | *Many thousands of years
test: Why can no person live a millennium? | Because people never get older than 50 | *Because a millennium is far longer than any human life | Because the oldest people live about 120 years | Because millennium means ten years
test: «The turn of the millennium» most likely means | A period of ten years | A very long walk | *The moment a new thousand years starts | A tree that is 4,000 years old
exam: If a timeline shows 3,000 years, how many millennia is that? | *3 | 1 | 10 | 30
